  "title": "Casa di San Giorgio (Bank of Saint George), Genoa",
  "summary": "Founded in Genoa in 1407 by consolidating farm revenues and public debt, the Casa di San Giorgio stayed separate from the Genoese government yet came to dominate its politics and control much of the city-state. It ran a public bank of deposit and transfer, lent to the state and governed overseas colonies until 1805.",
